Tieka wrote on Sun, 01 Feb 2004 14:00:52 -0500:
> problem is a lack of useable altars
[...]
> As I see it, I have three choices:

> a) keep going down carefully, and hope for an aligned altar later.

If you don't have a pressing need, that's what I'd do.

> b) Kill a priest, then convert an altar 

It's usually better to first desecrate the altar. Otherwise the God
of the temple might not like your meddling with their priest.

> c) Attempt to convert an altar, then kill priest if needed.

You'll need magic resistance and/or a ring of free action if you want
to take out the priest face to face or you risk getting paralysed.

Another (and for your character it seems--better) possibilty is to
take them out from outside the temple (in this case, don't convert the
altar before murdering the priest). Dig some of the walls and ensure
you have quite a lot of ammo--the priest won't leave the temple, but
may summon some bugs at you.

Of course, there's also
d) Make holy water by reading a blessed scroll of remove curse while
confused.

